            <ArticleTitle>Heel pain: diagnosis and management.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>380-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Chronic non-traumatic heel pain is not an uncommon symptom in patients presenting to GP, orthopaedic or rheumatological clinics. A full history and examination will provide a diagnosis in most cases. Rarer causes need to be excluded in certain patients. This article outlines the differential diagnosis and discusses the more common causes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
